# Personal use only, not for distribution or resale; not for navigation.
#
# EVERY TEXT FILE IS CHECKED OUT WITH LF, ON EVERY MACHINE.
#
# Ryan's Windows checkout has core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh checkout or worktree writes CRLF. Tests
# that read source or fixtures with a regex written for "\n" then fail there and nowhere else:
# nc-striped-bass.test.js and one-launch-source.test.js failed in every fresh worktree used to review
# a PR (2026-09-24/25), and a-fact-has-the-date-of-its-text.test.js did before its reader was patched.
# Patching each reader fixes one test; this fixes the checkout. The repository already stores LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows' own script hosts, left in the line ending they are written for.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
